    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my ac unit outside is making this weird humming noise but the fan isnt actually spinning. is there something wrong with it? also what should i look out for before i go poking around it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, a humming noise with a non-spinning fan usually means the motor is receiving power but can't start—often due to a faulty capacitor, a seized bearing, or a broken belt. Start by turning off the power at the breaker and the disconnect box near the unit before touching anything. Then, visually check for debris blocking the fan, look for bulging/leaking capacitors, and carefully try spinning the fan blade by hand (power off) to see if it moves freely. If the blade spins easily but still won’t start on its own, the capacitor is the likely culprit—call a pro if you're not comfortable replacing electrical parts.",
      "source": "target",
