    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just weird because it was working fine yesterday and now it's just making this constant buzzing/humming sound like it's struggling. it almost feels like something is just stuck in there or causing a glitch in the electrical part. any idea why it would just suddenly act up like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A sudden failure like this is very common with capacitors—they degrade over time and often die without warning, especially after a hot day when they’ve been under heavy load. The buzzing is the motor trying to start but failing, which usually points to a capacitor that can't provide the jolt anymore, or a seized bearing that finally gave out. Electrical components like capacitors can also fail instantly due to a power surge or brief voltage drop. Just remember to rule out the simple stuff first—like a leaf or twig jamming the blade—before assuming it's electrical.",
